    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener>
                    <dateline><date when="1947-05-22">May 22, 1947</date></dateline><salute>Dear <rs
                            ref="#tillich_person_id__4970" type="person">Dr. Jacobsen</rs>,</salute>
                </opener>
                <p><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4971" type="person">Mr. Hubert Fergus Thomson, Jr.</rs>
                    was a student at Union during the years, 1941–1943. He did very capable work in
                    the department of Systematic Theology, where I had him as a student. According
                    to the Registrar&apos;s office, the same was true of his work in other
                    departments.</p>
                <p><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4971" type="person">Mr. Thomson</rs> is very thorough
                    and competent in his work. His strong point is his scholarship rather than his
                    originality.</p>
                <closer>
                    <salute>Sincerely yours,</salute>
                    <signed>
                        <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Paul
                        Tillich</rs><lb/>Department of Systematic Theology</signed>
                </closer>

            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
